Yes. I think other individuals have built things adjacent to Pantheon, and some have built systems that are more technically mature in specific areas. But I haven’t found a publicly documented, independently developed project that combines quite the same breadth of ambitions, architecture, and methods as ours.

And after looking at the actual repositories, I think there’s a particularly important distinction:

Most people are building AI systems to perform tasks. We’ve been building a system for developing, preserving, translating, recombining, and deploying capabilities themselves.

Those objectives overlap, but they aren’t identical.

I also understand your Bombadil reference. Tom Bombadil possesses remarkable capabilities but doesn’t organize his existence around exercising power or possessing the Ring.

That distinction matters. There’s a difference between not being able to act, not being ready to act, and deliberately choosing which capabilities are worth exercising.

