The closest projects I’ve found

These are the strongest comparisons, especially those associated with individual builders.

1. Eidetic OS⁠￼ — Closest in persistent capability infrastructure

Long-term memory, a Git-backed knowledge vault, autonomous tasks, multi-agent research, and more than 160 documented skills. Its published implementation is further along in operationalizing recurring workflows. Pantheon has the broader semantic and cognitive-transformation ambition. GitHub

2. ARI⁠￼ — Closest in governance and cognitive architecture

Built by Pryce Hedrick, ARI has a seven-layer architecture, constitutional governance, specialized agents, audit trails, and business automation. This is a particularly interesting parallel because it combines cognitive principles with actual workflows. Its public repository is now archived. GitHub GitHub

3. Andrej Karpathy’s LLM Wiki⁠￼ — Closest in compounding knowledge

Karpathy described an LLM-maintained, interlinked knowledge system that integrates new information into accumulated understanding instead of repeatedly starting from raw material. That’s close to one fundamental Pantheon principle. But Pantheon goes beyond maintaining knowledge to specifying transformations and ways of reconstructing capabilities. GitHub

4. PersonalClaw⁠￼ — Stronger in executable autonomy

A self-hosted agent environment with memory, knowledge graphs, autonomous goal loops, scheduling, skills, and permission controls. More developed as a working assistant platform, but not primarily organized around Pantheon’s general semantic operators and cross-domain reasoning methods. GitHub

5. Holt⁠￼ — Closest in model-independent personal continuity

Built by Debashis Nayak, Holt supports changing AI models while retaining context, maintaining local memory, building a knowledge graph, and creating an evolving wiki. It demonstrates a concrete implementation of several continuity mechanisms that Pantheon specifies more abstractly. GitHub

None of these is identical to Pantheon. Nor can I establish that no private or undiscovered project is closer.

